We can rewrite the expression as
\begin{align*}
\log_{y^6}{x}\cdot\log_{x^5}{y^2}\cdot\log_{y^4}{x^3}\cdot\log_{x^3}{y^4}\cdot\log_{y^2}{x^5} &= \frac{\log{x}}{\log{y^6}}\cdot\frac{\log{y^2}}{\log{x^5}}\cdot\frac{\log{x^3}}{\log{y^4}}\cdot\frac{\log{y^4}}{\log{x^3}}\cdot\frac{\log{x^5}}{\log{y^2}} \\
&= \frac{\log{x}}{6\log{y}}\cdot\frac{2\log{y}}{5\log{x}}\cdot\frac{3\log{x}}{4\log{y}}\cdot\frac{4\log{y}}{3\log{x}}\cdot\frac{5\log{x}}{2\log{y}} \\
&= \frac{120\log{x}\log{y}}{720\log{x}\log{y}} \\
&= \frac{120}{720} \\
&= \frac{1}{6}.
\end{align*}
Therefore, $a = \boxed{\frac{1}{6}}.$
The answer is: \frac{1}{6}

